# rt_witness.ckir - CEIR-19c STAGE-1 WITNESS: the trivial one-ray_query inline-rayQuery kernel proving the ceir.rt->gpu
# execution bridge (execute_rt_lowered + dispatch_inline_ray_query) end-to-end on the device. AUTHORED (mandate #1: NO C++
# builder; the .ckir is the SOLE source, authored/edited DIRECTLY). Per launch index i: read ray i (6 f32: origin.xyz +
# dir.xyz) from the rays SSBO, inline-ray-query the TLAS, write the closest-hit distance t (F32) + the primitive index (U32).
# BINDING CONTRACT (REN-38-A9, dispatch_inline_ray_query): TLAS implicit @ descriptor 0; SSBOs by binding-operand order:
#   rays @ 1 (read, 6 f32/thread), hit_t @ 2 (write, F32), hit_prim @ 3 (write, U32). hit_prim is a U32 buffer, NEVER F32:
#   the 0xFFFFFFFF miss sentinel is unrepresentable in F32 (rounds to 2^32) and would break the bit-exact prim-id compare.
# GATE: the AS slot binds the real TLAS on the GPU and the triangle-soup oracle buffer (data[0]=ntri, then 9 f32/tri) for
# eval_cpu_kernel's TraceRayHit; hit-miss + prim-id are BIT-EXACT GPU==oracle, t is tolerance-class (unrounded-f64 oracle).
